SUMMARY:Webinar: Federal Research Investments in Whole Child Health and Wellbeing
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by the Decade of the Child Committee from the National Prevention Science Coalition to Improve Lives\, this free full-day event will feature leadership from the National Institutes of Health (NIH) and nationally recognized child health and wellbeing experts discussing how decades of scientific research can be translated into effective policies\, programs\, and practices that help children and families flourish. \nAs communities across the country work to improve outcomes for children and families\, this timely conversation will focus on how research investments can help identify\, implement\, scale\, and sustain evidence-based approaches that support lifelong success. \nJoin the sessions that fit your schedule; all registrants will receive recordings and event materials. \nSee the sessions and register here.
URL:https://resilientdurhamnc.org/event/webinar-federal-research-investments-in-whole-child-health-and-wellbeing/
LOCATION:Zoom
END:VEVENT
